join ember (normal) right [animation="Fade In"]
ember: Oh! Hello there.
ember: I wasn't expecting anyone to actually show up today.
ember: Sorry, that came out weird. I just meant... it's nice to see a new face.
ember: So, tell me. What brings you here?
[wait time="0.1"]
- You!
	ember (smug): Aww. That's forward, but I'll take it. (+20 Charm)
	[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"charm":20}"]
	ember: So, forward and direct. I like that combination. Are you always like this?
	- Only when I mean it.
		ember: Oh, now that's just unfair. (+10 Charm)
		[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"charm":10}"]
	- Only around people worth being direct with.
		ember: That's a good line. I might steal it. (+10 Wit)
		[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"wit":10}"]
- I'm here to be with someone very special...
	ember: Hmmm. I wonder who that could be. (+20 Wit)
	[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"wit":20}"]
	ember: You're going to keep me guessing all day, aren't you.
	- Maybe. Keeps things interesting.
		ember: I do like interesting. (+10 Wit)
		[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"wit":10}"]
	- I could just tell you, if you want.
		ember: No, no — let me have the mystery a little longer. (+10 Charm)
		[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"charm":10}"]
- I want to defend you.
	ember: That's... surprisingly sincere for a first hello. (Vulnerability risk)
	do GameManager.apply_vulnerability_risk(20, 0.55)
	if {last_vulnerability_success} == true:
		ember: Most people lead with a joke. You led with a promise. I like that more than I expected to.
	else:
		ember (sad): That's... a lot of sincerity for a first hello. I don't know what to do with that yet.
	- I don't make promises I can't keep.
		ember: I'm going to hold you to that. (+10 Trust)
		[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"trust":10}"]
	- I just say what I mean.
		ember: That's rarer than you'd think. (+10 Wit)
		[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"wit":10}"]
ember: Well, whatever brought you here, I'm glad you came.
ember: Something tells me it's about to get busy, though.
do GameManager.end_dialogue()